  rn.stats()             # captures, recaptures, evictions, last_capture_s, key, n_graphs, E_caps

KEY POLICY (documented choice: transparent separate graph, never raise, never cross-replay)
  key = (n_atoms, atoms.numbers.tobytes(), pbc tuple, cell-all-zero, calc.head, model dtype, stress flag)
  Per key one graph in an LRU OrderedDict (max_graphs=4; least-recently-used graph freed). A new key -> capture at
  round_cap(E, 0.20, 64). E > E_cap -> brand-new graph object at round_cap(E, 0.25) (all bookkeeping rebuilt: N, E_cap,
  pad indices, statics, node_attrs, batch/ptr, outputs); old one freed. Before replay: host np.array_equal(numbers)
  check; per-node statics refreshed by copy_ if the batch passes tensors other than those captured from (shape-checked).
STRESS: supported (stress=True). MACE builds displacement internally (captured); grads wrt (positions, displacement)
  captured. Padded edges get unit_shift (m,0,0), m=max(1,ceil(2 r_max/|cell[0]|)) computed on GPU per load, because
  MACE recomputes shifts = unit_shifts @ displaced cell. Non-periodic systems return stress 0 exactly like eager.

